xnu 0445: acknowledge the PBL BHI interrupt before the doorbell

Measured 2026-11-26 with the boot-time auto-load (mondrianwififw=1,
mondrianwifidelay=0): the 0444 reset and the BHI trigger run seconds after W1
releases PERST, and BHI_STATUS still reads 0x0 after 10000 polls. The PBL
never fetches, so the trigger itself is not reaching it.

Three differences from mhi_fw_load_bhi remain. It never writes BHI_INTVEC, it
rings BHI_IMGTXDB with a 30-bit sequence number, and the MHI interrupt handler
reads BHI_EXECENV after the reset to decode and acknowledge the PBL
transition. Preserve INTVEC, log it, read EXECENV before the doorbell, and use
0x2a5a5a5a instead of 1. The existing interrupt clear runs before the SOC
reset; the reset clears the block and the PBL raises its ready interrupt
afterwards, so clear the endpoint's interrupt status again before asking for
the image.

